# The build context is the repository root, because the relay workspace depends on
# crates/sluice-meet by path. Only what the two workspaces and the image need goes in: a target/
# folder, a local config, a certificate or a key never reaches the build. The guard's tests are left
# out too, and the relay's own tests, because the image builds the two binaries.
*
!crates/sluice-meet/Cargo.toml
!crates/sluice-meet/words.txt
!crates/sluice-meet/src
!docker/guard/Cargo.toml
!docker/guard/Cargo.lock
!docker/guard/src
!docker/relay-server/Cargo.toml
!docker/relay-server/Cargo.lock
!docker/relay-server/src
!docker/relay/relay.toml
!docker/relay/open.toml
!docker/relay/meeting-point.toml
docker/guard/src/tests.rs
docker/guard/src/tests
docker/relay-server/tests
